  {
    "name": "game_manage",
    "title": "Game Manage",
    "description": "Runtime game inspection and input simulation.\n\nThese ops target the running game process through Godot's EngineDebugger\nbridge. Start the project first with project_run and poll editor_state until\ngame_capture_ready=true.\n\nOps:\n  - get_scene_tree(depth=10, root_path=\"\")\n        Inspect the running scene tree. root_path accepts an absolute runtime\n        path or a scene-relative path rooted at the current scene.\n  - get_node_info(path, include_properties=True)\n        Inspect one running node's metadata and optional property snapshot.\n  - get_ui_elements(root_path=\"\", include_hidden=False,\n                    include_disabled=True, max_depth=10)\n        Inspect visible runtime Control nodes for UI testing. Includes path,\n        type, text where present, disabled state, and rect metadata.\n  - suspend()\n        Suspend the running game through Godot's native debugger path.\n  - resume()\n        Resume a suspended game. Idempotent when it is already running.\n  - next_frame()\n        Advance exactly one process tick while suspended. The response reports\n        verification and any Embedded Game View focus handoff. Runtime-control\n        mutations also report path=\"embed_signal\" or \"direct_session\"; the\n        direct fallback works without embedding but cannot synchronize the\n        Game View suspend button's visual pressed state.\n  - debug_status()\n        Probe suspend state and the game-helper process tick counter through\n        the debugger capture, including while SceneTree processing is suspended.\n  - input_key(key, pressed=True, echo=False)\n        Send a key press/release to the running game.\n  - input_mouse(event, position=None, button=\"left\", pressed=True)\n        Send a mouse motion or button event. event: \"motion\" | \"button\".\n        position is a {x, y} object or [x, y] array; omit it to use the\n        game's current cursor position. A present but malformed position is\n        rejected rather than silently falling back to the cursor.\n  - input_gamepad(device=0, control=\"button\", index=0, pressed=True, value=0.0)\n        Send a joypad button or axis event. control: \"button\" | \"axis\".\n  - input_action(action, pressed=True, strength=1.0)\n        Set a project action's pressed state directly in the running game.\n  - input_sequence(steps, settle_frames=0)\n        Apply a frame-timed action timeline in one call \u2014 the frame-accurate,\n        multi-step form of input_action. Each step is\n        {at_frame, action, pressed=True, strength=1.0}; the game applies each\n        step's action on its scheduled frame, awaits settle_frames more, then\n        replies once. Use this instead of separate input_action calls whenever\n        timing matters (jump arcs, combos, walk-into-trigger): per-call network\n        latency makes hitting a target frame impossible otherwise. Steps must\n        be ordered by non-decreasing at_frame; frames (not ms) are the timing\n        basis. Action-based input is focus-independent, so it works on a\n        backgrounded game window. Cannot run inside batch_execute.\n  - input_state(actions=None)\n        Read current action pressed states. Empty actions = all project actions.\n\nCanonical call shape: ``{\"op\": \"<verb>\", \"params\": {...}}``. Flat op parameters are accepted as a compatibility alias when the client transmits them; ``op`` and ``session_id`` remain top-level.",
    "input_schema": {
      "properties": {
        "op": {
          "enum": [
            "debug_status",
            "get_node_info",
            "get_scene_tree",
            "get_ui_elements",
            "input_action",
            "input_gamepad",
            "input_key",
            "input_mouse",
            "input_sequence",
            "input_state",
            "next_frame",
            "resume",
            "suspend"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "params": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "additionalProperties": true,
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "session_id": {
          "default": "",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "op"
      ],
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "execution": null,
    "output_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true
    },
    "icons": null,
    "annotations": null,
    "meta": {
      "defer_loading": true,
      "fastmcp": {
        "tags": []
      }
    }
  }
